{
  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "1) Evidence: config_007 (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted + multiprofile) achieved 0.635 acc, a dramatic ~9-point jump over config_019 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l, same other settings) at 0.542. This strongly implicates the RNA encoder as the dominant factor. However, we also know imagenet_vit_l modestly outperforms resnet50 with scgpt (config_019: 0.542 vs config_048: 0.525). 2) Question: config_006 (pca_n2000 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted + multiprofile) is a single-variable swap of the image encoder from imagenet_vit_l to resnet50, directly comparing against config_007. This isolates whether the 0.635 result is driven primarily by the RNA representation (pca_n2000) or requires the specific combination with imagenet_vit_l. 3) Why best next experiment: This is the cleanest, most informative single-variable test from the current best configuration. If pca_n2000 + resnet50 performs comparably, it confirms the RNA encoder is the key lever and the image encoder is secondary—guiding all future experiments toward RNA representation choices. If it drops substantially, it reveals a critical interaction effect. Either outcome sharply reduces uncertainty about which design axis to prioritize under a limited budget, making this the highest-information-value experiment available."
}

